  COMMENTS                    :
             transducer temperature/soundspeed correction:
             Comparison ADCP temperature and temperature from Thermo-Salino;
             apply an offset -0.22 on ADCP temperature from the decimal day 200.
             Salinity from Thermo-Salino is interpolated on ADCP time.  

             Wire interference:
             The error velocity did indicate sections where the CTD wire
             may have interfered with the ADCP.  It seems to affect a wider
             bin range from around bin 5 down to bin 20 (or more) at times.
             The bad bins were flagged using the program badbin, before
             the flagging program was run again for the amplitude, etc. passes.

             Bottom editing:
             The last blocks:profiles (86:47 to 88:50) have bogus data,
             collected in port, shallow water. They have been deleted.
             All the flags are noisier than usual because the data
             collection was done with four-meters bins.

