CALIBRATION 
    GYROCOMPASS CORRECTION      : YES 
            The following describes the calibration done using ashtech:
 
            In most of cases, the heading error is obtained by a 10 minutes
            median filter Ashtech data interpolation on ADCP time (here, Ashtech
            data mean "one-minute mean (ashtech - gyro) heading").
            When there are some "big" gaps in the Ashtech data, a gyro model
            is used to fill them. In fact, three models are used depending on the
            velocity compensation, assuming an once per day latitude update
            + model 1: no velocity compensation
            + model 2: constant velocity compensation (10 knots)
            + model 3: velocity compensation when underway only
            However, for some time-ranges, none of these models work well. In
            these cases, the gyro model is simply an linear interpolation of
            10 minutes median filter Ashtech data.
            WHAT I DID:
            + linear interpolation of 10 minutes median filter Ashtech data:
              time-range 190.6 to 190.6 about
              time-range 220.5 to 221.05 about
            + gyro model:
              time-range 209.93 to 210.52 about --> model 2 with an offset +1
              time-range 215.09 to 216.09 about --> model 2 with an offset +1.6
              time-range 217.47 to 217.99 about --> model 1 with an offset +1.4

